# Shell scripts run on macOS and Linux. This repository is configured with
# core.autocrlf=true, so without this rule a Windows checkout writes them with
# CRLF, the first line becomes `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` and Linux looks for an
# interpreter whose name ends in a carriage return (measured in SymDiary). The
# Flatpak and DMG builders would then fail on the platforms they exist for.
*.sh text eol=lf
